## Last-In-First-Out with Stack

A **stack** is a LIFO (Last In, First Out) data structure. Items are added and removed from the same end — the "top" of the stack.

### Building a Stack with Vec

```xiom
pub type Stack[T] = { items: Vec[T]; }

fn Stack.new[T]() -> Stack[T] {
  return Stack{ items: Vec[T]() };
}

fn Stack.push[T](self: &mut Stack[T], item: T) -> Unit {
  self.items.push(item);
}

fn Stack.pop[T](self: &mut Stack[T]) -> Option[T] {
  return self.items.pop();
}

fn Stack.peek[T](self: &Stack[T]) -> Option[T] {
  if self.items.len() == 0 { return None; }
  return Some(self.items[self.items.len() - 1]);
}
```

### Using a Stack

```xiom
var s = Stack[Int].new();
s.push(1);
s.push(2);
s.push(3);  // stack: [1, 2, 3] — top is 3

let top = s.peek();   // Some(3) — look without removing
let val = s.pop();    // Some(3) — remove top
let val2 = s.pop();   // Some(2)
```

### LIFO Behavior

```
push(1):  [1]            top=1
push(2):  [1, 2]         top=2
push(3):  [1, 2, 3]      top=3
pop():    [1, 2]   → 3
pop():    [1]      → 2
pop():    []       → 1
```

### Practical Uses

- **Undo/Redo**: push state on each action; pop to undo
- **Expression evaluation**: parse math expressions
- **Backtracking**: maze solving, pathfinding
- **Function call stack**: compiler tracks calls

### Stack Operations

| Operation | Return | Description |
|-----------|--------|-------------|
| push(item) | Unit | Add to top |
| pop() | Option[T] | Remove from top |
| peek() | Option[T] | Look at top |
| len() | Int | Number of items |
| is_empty() | Bool | Check if empty |

